course: dictionary
lesson: 10593
title: Undersea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Undersea is a word made of two parts, under and sea. It means below the surface of the sea, or happening under the sea. Look at the words around it to check. «Most data between continents travels through undersea cables, not satellites.» Cables that travel between continents must be under the sea, so undersea means below the surface.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put below the surface of the sea in place of undersea: «Most data between continents travels through below-the-sea cables» sounds clumsy, but the meaning still fits. If your swap makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Undersea usually describes a thing, like a volcano, a cable or a tunnel. An undersea volcano is a volcano that is below the sea. The word tells you where something is, so it helps you picture it.
fact: Undersea means below the surface of the sea, or happening under the sea.
fact: «Undersea earthquake» means an earthquake that happens under the sea.
fact: «Tsunami» means a series of huge waves, usually caused by a sudden movement of a lot of water, such as an undersea earthquake.
fact: A tsunami is not one giant surfing wave. It is a series of huge waves.
fact: «Undersea cables» carry data between continents. Inside, thin glass fibres carry pulses of light.
exercise: «Most data between continents travels through undersea cables, not satellites.» What does undersea mean here? | Inside a spaceship | *Below the surface of the sea | On top of a mountain | Above the clouds
exercise: «Scientists studied an undersea volcano.» Find and copy the word that describes the volcano. | volcano | studied | scientists | *undersea
exercise: «An undersea tunnel» is a tunnel where? | In the mountains | *Below the sea | On a ship's deck | In a desert
test: «A tsunami is a series of huge waves caused by something suddenly moving a lot of water, usually an undersea earthquake.» What usually causes a tsunami? | *An undersea earthquake | A sunny day at the beach | A strong wind on land | A giant surfing wave
test: «If a ship's anchor cuts one undersea cable, data goes round by the others, maybe more slowly.» What happens to the data? | *It goes round by the other cables, maybe more slowly | It stops for ever | It goes up into satellites and is lost | The sea water drains away
exam: Which phrase means a volcano below the sea? | A sunny beach | A volcano in the desert | *An undersea volcano | A mountain volcano
